  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.07,
      "end_seconds": 3.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Alright, evening. Let's get started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.37,
      "end_seconds": 8.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "hi there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.56,
      "end_seconds": 15.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "good afternoon, doctor i look after them so I thought I'd come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.74,
      "end_seconds": 23.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "good, that'll be useful pull up a chair what do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 24.22,
      "end_seconds": 27.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "he's been having a headache, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.22,
      "end_seconds": 36.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.8,
      "text": "Oh, I was just going to to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 36.12,
      "end_seconds": 42.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.23,
      "end_seconds": 46.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "later, thanks. Please go on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.4,
      "end_seconds": 54.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "Oh, and being drowsy. I've also been feeling sick, since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.85,
      "end_seconds": 63.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "how strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.78,
      "end_seconds": 67.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "About a three out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.51,
      "end_seconds": 73.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Have you had a headache before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.64,
      "end_seconds": 80.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "a bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 82.3,
      "end_seconds": 85.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "yes, that's right, that's how it was"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.78,
      "end_seconds": 90.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "And what about chest pain, rash or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.87,
      "end_seconds": 97.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "oh, no chest pain, rash or fever, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.78,
      "end_seconds": 99.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.39,
      "end_seconds": 104.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "that's normal as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.22,
      "end_seconds": 109.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.12,
      "end_seconds": 112.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "no problems with breathing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.71,
      "end_seconds": 118.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.42,
      "end_seconds": 122.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "not to my knowledge, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 124.26,
      "end_seconds": 130.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with amoxicillin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.5,
      "end_seconds": 134.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.39,
      "end_seconds": 140.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.43,
      "end_seconds": 157.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.86,
      "end_seconds": 162.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "my father had bowel cancer my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.39,
      "end_seconds": 168.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.41,
      "end_seconds": 174.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "I'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.82,
      "end_seconds": 175.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.91,
      "end_seconds": 185.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.06,
      "end_seconds": 189.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.18,
      "end_seconds": 199.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "For the stent, I believe. My daughter sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.35,
      "end_seconds": 205.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.09,
      "end_seconds": 212.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "yes, I had my tonsils removed, as a teenager"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.66,
      "end_seconds": 217.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.66,
      "end_seconds": 221.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I've had heart failure, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.78,
      "end_seconds": 223.48,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.07,
      "end_seconds": 226.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "I have heart disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.1,
      "end_seconds": 233.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "yes, heart disease is known to us, good to have that clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.35,
      "end_seconds": 244.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "what does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.91,
      "end_seconds": 249.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 250.8,
      "end_seconds": 255.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pressure 125 over 77, pulse 84."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.62,
      "end_seconds": 258.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.75,
      "end_seconds": 264.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.94,
      "end_seconds": 268.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.62,
      "end_seconds": 291.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.9,
      "text": "Your lips are pink but the whole household feels unwell, and the oxygen reading looks normal but cannot be trusted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.79,
      "end_seconds": 318.77,
      "duration_seconds": 22.98,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is possible carbon monoxide poisoning. We shouldn't forget a viral illness. I'm prescribing high-flow oxygen, 15 litres per minute, continuous, until reviewed. That should help with carbon monoxide poisoning. Alright, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.25,
      "end_seconds": 323.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "good, thanks, I'll see you then"
    }
  ]
}